# PART III — PRODUCT VISION

## 7. What The Shred Roadmap is intended to become

The Shred Roadmap is a premium, comprehensive music-learning and musicianship application.

It must not become:

- A simple quiz application.
- A shallow guitar course.
- An XP-driven game.
- A collection of disconnected tools.
- A superficial collection of theory definitions.

The learner is a musician first and a guitarist second.

General music theory and musicianship form the foundation. Guitar-specific fluency is a practical application layer.

The application should help the learner:

- Understand music theory from foundational to advanced levels.
- Develop deep fretboard knowledge and practical fluency.
- Understand harmony and analyse complex music.
- Improvise freely instead of depending exclusively on memorised shapes.
- Compose riffs, progressions, solos and complete pieces.
- Connect theoretical knowledge to listening, musical decisions and practical execution.
- Develop genuine musical independence.

The desired editorial depth is encyclopaedic and almost academic, while remaining readable, practical and carefully structured.

Do not sacrifice educational depth for superficial gamification or short attention-span interactions.

## 8. Musical context

Important musical reference worlds include:

- Stoner.
- Doom.
- Sludge.
- Progressive music.
- Death metal.
- Thrash.
- Blues.
- Selected classic rock.

These are useful musical contexts, but the curriculum must remain broad and musically rigorous.

Do not restrict music theory to guitar or to a narrow selection of genres.

